A Laravel app has a custom LoginController whose login() method does exactly this:

```php
public function login(Request $request)
{
    $credentials = $request->validate(['email' => 'required|email', 'password' => 'required']);
    if (Auth::attempt($credentials)) {
        Auth::login(Auth::user());
        return redirect('/dashboard');
    }
    return back()->withErrors(['email' => 'Invalid credentials']);
}
```

It bypasses Laravel's built-in AuthenticatesUsers trait. What security issue does this introduce and what line should be added to fix it?

